    <div class="landing-page">
      <div class="landing-content">

        <!-- PensionTools' questions, the site's front page since 7.0 (usability audit decision 8): one line, at the top, before anything else; the simple view's front door, with the hash so it never forwards back here (7.11.0) -->
        <p class="landing-new"><a href="${nr.classic.v7}#/" id="landingPreviewLink">The simple view: answer one question in about two minutes</a></p>

        <!-- Hero -->
        <div class="landing-hero">
          <h1>${Wv}</h1>
          <p class="landing-tagline">Plan your retirement with confidence</p>
          <p class="landing-subtitle">Free tools to work out what your retirement will actually cost, stress-test whether your pension can pay for it, and decide where to draw from each month.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- The flow in one line -->
        <p class="landing-flow">What will it cost? <span>&#8594;</span> Will the money last? <span>&#8594;</span> What do I draw this month?</p>

        <!-- Tools overview -->
        <div class="landing-tools">
          <div class="landing-tool-card">
            <div class="landing-step-badge">Step 1</div>
            <div class="landing-tool-icon">&#x1F9FE;</div>
            <h3>Budget Planner</h3>
            <p class="landing-tool-question">"What will retirement actually cost?"</p>
            <p>A guided walk-through of your real spending — bills to holidays to the car you'll replace every few years — with typical UK figures when you're unsure. Couples can split who pays what. When you are ready, one button uses it as your plan's spending.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="landing-tool-card">
            <div class="landing-step-badge">Step 2</div>
            <div class="landing-tool-icon">&#x1F4CA;</div>
            <h3>Stress Tester</h3>
            <p class="landing-tool-question">"Can I afford to retire?"</p>
            <p>Run 1,000 simulations using real historical market data. See how your pension holds up under crashes, inflation, and different spending levels.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="landing-tool-card">
            <div class="landing-step-badge">Step 3</div>
            <div class="landing-tool-icon">&#x1F4B7;</div>
            <h3>Monthly Decisions</h3>
            <p class="landing-tool-question">"Which pot could this month's money come from?"</p>
            <p>Each month, see what taking it from shares, bonds or cash does to your tax and your pots.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="landing-section">
          <h2>Still saving? There's a tool for that too</h2>
          <p>The <strong>Accumulation Planner</strong> works the same net-first way for the years
          before retirement: say what you can spare from take-home pay, and it works out the gross
          pension purchase under your scheme's tax relief, projects your pot, and checks whether
          you're on course for your own budget-derived target — not a rule of thumb.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Why use this -->
        <div class="landing-section">
          <h2>What you'll need</h2>
          <p>Just a few basic numbers — your ages, roughly what you spend, and your pension fund values. Everything works in take-home terms: you say what you want in your pocket each month and the tax is handled for you. No gross-salary puzzles, and no sensitive data like account numbers or passwords.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="landing-section">
          <h2>Your data stays private</h2>
          <p>Your settings are stored securely in the cloud (Google Firebase) and only you can access them. Nothing is shared, sold, or visible to anyone else. Sign in from any device to pick up where you left off.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="landing-section">
          <h2>Beta — a work in progress</h2>
          <p>Built and run by Usefulish Ltd, and still changing week to week. Numbers move as the models improve; nothing here is financial advice. If something looks wrong, it may well be.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="landing-feature">
          <h2>Completely free</h2>
          <p>All tools are free to use. No ads, no premium tier, no catch. We built it to help people make better pension decisions.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- CTA -->
        <div class="landing-cta">
          <button class="landing-btn primary" id="landingGetStarted">Get Started — Create Free Account</button>
          <button class="landing-btn secondary" id="landingSignIn">Already have an account? Sign In</button>
          ${s?'<button class="landing-btn secondary" id="landingTryGuest" title="The plans you made in this browser window without an account are still here until you close it">Carry on with the plans in this window — no account</button>':'<button class="landing-btn secondary" id="landingTryGuest" title="Start your own plan with no account. '+$v+'">Just try it — no account needed</button>'}
          <button class="landing-btn secondary" id="landingLookAround" title="A finished example plan to look around: £1M, £40,000 a year. It cannot be changed.">Look around an example</button>
          <p class="landing-guest-note">Without an account: ${$v}</p>
        </div>

        <div class="landing-footer">
          <p><a href="${nr.classic.privacy}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Privacy Policy</a> &middot; Usefulish Ltd</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
